	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10176"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=309" title="View the profile of Roinin">Roinin</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 16<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								I&#039;m a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=309"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=840.msg10176#msg10176"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=840.msg10176#msg10176">Re: Rant re Ialin on Hegemony Raid</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #58 on:</b> August 18, 2004, 08:35:22 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Sure, I&#039;ll reply to this thread.&nbsp; Being a little late for the replies, but&nbsp; a reply none the less. Seeing as I was the Raid Leader that day. So, if anyone to vent your muted hopes of&nbsp; conquering&nbsp; your first Grummus kill, then that would be myself. Let&#039;s start out proper, shall we? First, I am Roinin, officer and raid leader (one of) for Hegemony. I don&#039;t read this board much, but recently sifting through some of the more recent threads here, I&#039;ve noticed there have been many complants or comments of pre elemental targets not being very available. Albiet true, I can attest for this phenomenon myself, always seeking out targets to help my guild progress onward.<br /><br />Now, possibly to give a little background information to help fill in any doubts or blanks that anyone has, Hegemony have been feverishly recruiting and backflagging for the past&nbsp; couple of recent months. We have done this to get out of a slump that all guilds progressing through the elementals have had to do before their push towards time.&nbsp; I would go into the phenomenon more, but I think it&#039;s rather irrelevant on when or why this happens. Our guild&nbsp; on a near nightly basis, thouroughly sought out progression for our newest addidtions to our ranks. We seek to flag our members fully, so that they can raid with us unhindered by the 85 situation.&nbsp; Now, we could quite possibly raid&nbsp; purely Elemental zones and eternally 85 in our more recent applicants, but..&nbsp; That is not our goals or intentions. We need and want these players to have&nbsp; acces to everything we are currently doing, and to be able to enjoy these zones whenever they&nbsp; like.<br />We raid and progress because we enjoy&nbsp; it , all the while having tons of fun doing it. <br /><br />Now, Backflagging&nbsp; isn&#039;t really all that fun. I&#039;ll be frank and honest about it. When you&#039;ve killed the same mobs 2 dozen times, it does get a little stale. Part of our goal here, is to get this process done as quickly as possible, hitting anything and everything available to catch these new people up to speed with you. I can&#039;t tell you the thoughts that cross my mind or the facial expressions I get&nbsp; when considering hitting Grummus *again* for the 17634th time, or any number of the other lower teired PoP encounters.<br />The simple fact remains, for&nbsp; our recruits to progress, it is up to us to provide them with the flags they need to do so. It&#039;s simply manditory to progress. Thankfully, backflagging is dwinding down, there are very few targets we still actually neeed for flags, as we make a bold stride forward with&nbsp; &nbsp;3 impressive Elemental God kills/attempts in the past month alone.<br /><br />Now, on a more personal note. I was currently leading another raid in another zone, which at this time,&nbsp; I can&#039;t recall,&nbsp; perhaps it was something in tactics. I often run a little druid around during raids, to&nbsp; see what&#039;s available next so we can move seamlessly throughout the night. Granted there are other people&nbsp; that do this as well, but most we&#039;re not online this day. Before I even called the previous raid (Tactics? such a blur..) I had this druid parked in Disease at the zone in it&#039;s self. Grummus was actually considered before Tactics(?)&nbsp; but based on the number of flags needed at that current time, tactics was chosen first. Now, after Tactics ended,&nbsp; I look over&nbsp; onto the other comp and i see no one single person in Disease, I see Grummus is still up and fully available. So.. Logically, that&#039;s where we head.<br />Knowing nothing about there being 3 guilds camped outside, or nothing of anyone&#039;s prior plans, sitting <b> outside</b> of a zone.<br /><br />I had a client crash I recall, and decided to reboot to clear some lag after my comp had been on&nbsp; for 2 days. Nothing occured to me as I was reloading EQ about anyone else&#039;s intentions for the mob I just called. It&#039;s customary for&nbsp; us to meet at the&nbsp; firebone castle door, or even up top right by Gryme when we do grummus. Basically, as you&nbsp; may have seen, we intend to move as quickly as possible to get the job done. Grummus raid lasted about 20 minutes from start to finish.<br /><br />Now , had I previously known that there was a grummus attempt in progress, from <b> outside</b> the zone, I would of probly attempted to contace a raid leader or guild leader from the guilds there and see if we could arrange some sort of flagging arrangement. Not that it would of worked, I would of at least extended the courtesy perhaps.<br /><br />To you, Grummus may be a huge big kill, and you&#039;re all really psyched about it, as we once were&nbsp; quite a long time ago. In the present , for Hegemony anyways, it&#039;s&nbsp; simply veiwed as somemob_07 that we need to kill and move on to the next flagging mob. The loot isnt a factor, the fun of the encounter isnt, and trying to &quot;steal&quot; it away from someone surely isnt fun or a thing we practice for us either.<br />I rebooted (takes me a while) and the raid was already&nbsp; formed up and&nbsp; working on Gryme&#039;s guards, as I ran to the zone and got *lagged* by this massive collection of players sitting out front. I&#039;m wondering what&#039;s going on, but I don&#039;t stand around&nbsp; to ask questions.<br /><br />In short, I called the raid, seeing with eyes from inside the zone. No one was there.&nbsp; It was never my intent to run over anybody, and events happened quickly as I rebooted. My apologies for the misunderstand on my end as well as my guilds. Sure, had I known something was taking place already, events would of probly changed, and the outcome would probly be more amiacable between us. All, I&#039;m offering anyways is an explanation, I&#039;d&nbsp; hope it would suffice, but take or leave it at your own will.<br /><br />On a side note, could you perhaps form the raid &quot;inside&quot; the zone in the future? This could possibly help eliiminate any further confusion between any future guilds you may cross paths with.&nbsp; And it&#039;s an honest request, or a simple suggestion perhaps. Again, take it or leave it, just thought I&#039;d toss it out there.<br /><br />Good luck with Grummus if you havent already killed him by now, as well as your further ventures throughout the Planes of Power.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=266327" target="_blank">Roinin Unsleep</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10199"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=426" title="View the profile of Transhade">Transhade</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 15<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/skull4.png" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								A Shadowknight who believes he isn&#039;t useless<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=426"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=840.msg10199#msg10199"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=840.msg10199#msg10199">Re: Rant re Ialin on Hegemony Raid</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #59 on:</b> August 18, 2004, 12:51:19 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Generally as a rule and out of courtesy to those people who still grind in the planes,&nbsp; we do not zone in until we are set. I think everyone knows why.&nbsp; <br /><br />I was not leading the raid that day and acted only as a participant, but it seemed quite obvious that every other guild who thought of taking grummus down realized that 72 people sitting right next to the zone into PoD might mean that we were planning to raid there.<br /><br />Now I can understand wanting to keep raids moving, but it does seem a little weak that no one in Hegemony on the raid guessed that 72 people sitting outside the zone had some intentions in PoD.&nbsp; <br /><br />Of course, we accept the first to engage mob attitude exists, but it was nice to see that other guilds demonstrated the courtesy of&nbsp; communicating with the Raid Leader and deciding to allow this raid a shot at Grummus for the first time.<br /><br />On that night, the perception was Hegemony acted like a bunch of asses lacking any style or common courtesy.&nbsp; Being that some of your guild members have alts in Sons of Kings or relatives there, we know you aren&#039;t all bad.&nbsp; However, the perception of your guild has dropped apparently for many players on Rodcet Nife.&nbsp; Whether that matters to your guild or what you do with that information is up to your guild.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Duke Transhade Darkfuy<br />65th Level Shadowknight<br />Guild Leader Sons of Kings
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
